      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `otp_key_buffer` is allocated on the stack as a byte array. If the underlying `otp_read` or `otp_program` driver implementations cast this to a `uint32_t *` internally for word-aligned accesses (which is common for OTP/Flash controllers), this may result in an unaligned memory access fault.\n\nConsider forcing 4-byte alignment here just to be safe, since you already enforce `BUILD_ASSERT(OTP_KEY_SIZE_BYTES % 4 \u003d\u003d 0)` above:\n\n```c\n\tuint8_t __aligned(4) otp_key_buffer[OTP_KEY_SIZE_BYTES] \u003d { 0 };\n```",
